6. In the reference twelfth read above, the Registrar of Cooperative Societies has submitted a proposal to the Government for procurement of copra under Price Support Scheme (PSS) and requested orders of the Government.

7. As the current price of milling copra in open market is lower as compared to the Minimum Support Price (MSP), the Government for the benefit of farmers have decided to procure copra at the Minimum Support Price (MSP) at Rs.59.50 per kg for milling copra and at Rs.62.40 per kg for ball copra and accordingly issue orders for the procurement of copra under Price Support Scheme (PSS). The Government further order that –

i. Agriculture Department shall issue a Notification regarding expected production, sowing area, average yield, peak arrival/harvesting period for Copra and willingness to implement PSS ; ii. The copra procured by NAFED under Price Support Scheme (PSS) shall be exempted from levy of VAT (5%) and Agricultural Produce Market Committee (APMC) Cess (1%) . In this regard, necessary Notification / Orders will be issued by Commercial Taxes and Registration Department and Agriculture Department respectively ; iii. Necessary proposal for implementing Price Support Scheme (PSS) will be submitted by the Agriculture Department to Government of India;

iv. Tamil Nadu Co-operative Marketing Federation Limited (TANFED) will act as a State agency for procurement of copra and on receiving clearance from the Government of India, Tamil Nadu Co-operative Marketing Federation (TANFED) and National Agricultural Co-operative Marketing Federation of India Limited (NAFED), the Central agency will enter into an agreement followed by Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between TANFED and Primary Societies for opening Procurement Centres; v. Adequate number of procurement centres will be opened in the major coconut growing districts, namely, Coimbatore, Tiruppur, Erode, Thanjavur, Dindigul, Kanniyakumari, Vellore, Thoothukudi, Salem, Theni, Ramanathapuram, Tirunelveli, Dharmapuri, Krishnagiri, Sivagangai, Madurai, Nagapattinam, Namakkal, Pudukkottai and Tiruvarur based on the proposal from the respective District Collectors;

vi. Payment to Farmers shall be made directly to their bank accounts through ECS/Account Payee Cheque ;

/p.t.o./

/4/

vii. Government have already issued detailed guidelines for procurement of copra vide G.O.(Ms) No.134, Cooperation, Food and Consumer Protection Department, dated 14.07.2005 and issued certain amendments from time to time. In view of the guidelines issued by the Government of India, the Government orders certain amendments to the existing guidelines as detailed in Annexure to this order.

viii. Copra shall be procured only from genuine farmers.

ix. The Direct Procurement Centres shall commence with effect from 15.06.2016;

